<title>USA: EMU should fix FX rates early - Belgium's Maystadt.</title>
<headline>EMU should fix FX rates early - Belgium's Maystadt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Finance Minister Philippe Maystadt said on Tuesday he backed a proposal to fix exchange rates of currencies due to join European monetary union at the same time as a decision is made on which countries will join when the single currency is launched in 1999.</p>
<p>European Monetary Institute head Alexandre Lamfalussy has suggested this early fixing of exchange rates to prevent currency speculation in the run-up to monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;Personally I am in favour of Mr. Lamfalussy's proposal,&quot; Maystadt said in an interview with Reuters.</p>
<p>He said however that he could not say whether there was a consensus building among European countries to back the proposal.</p>
<p>European Union leaders must decide by June 1998 which countries will join a single currency when it is launched in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Myra MacDonald  IMF newsroom +1 202 745 0167</p>
